              alpha: 1,
              note: "Lipschitz with one kink ⇒ |⟨f, ψ_{j,k}⟩| ~ 2^{−3j/2} near the kink. Effective decay rate α = 1, so log₂|d| has slope α + ½ = 1.5 — exactly the Haar limit. Compression is good: only the few atoms adjacent to the kink matter."
            },
    smooth: { fn: x => Math.exp(-30*(x-0.5)*(x-0.5)),
              label: "Gaussian bump (C^∞)",
              alpha: 5,
              note: "C^∞ regularity would predict slope α + ½ = 5.5, but Haar has only 1 vanishing moment, so its coefficient decay saturates at slope min(α + ½, M + ½) = 1.5. The dashed yellow line is drawn at the *Haar* limit; with db4 (4 moments) we would see slope up to 4.5 here. This is why orthogonal wavelet families with more vanishing moments are preferred for smooth signals."
            }
  };
